  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      151.89,
      449.29,
      438.37,
      460.36
    ],
    "text": "to amend the Town and Country Planning Ordinance (Chapter 269)",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      240.31,
      291.47,
      359.47,
      300.33
    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      310.87,
      455.99,
      349.58
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause replaces the Long Title to the Town and Country PlanningOrdinance (Chapter 269) (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legaleffect of this amendment is to widen the scope of the activities which can be implementedunder the Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      360.31,
      455.99,
      399.14
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3 : This clause replaces section 2 of the principal enactment and the legal effect isto require the National Physical Council to prepare a National Physical Policy and aNational Physical Plan for the purpose of protecting and conserving the different categoriesof areas, which may be declared under the Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      409.87,
      455.84,
      428.78
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4 : This clause replaces section 6 of the principal enactment and the legal effect isto enhance the scope of the Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      439.51,
      455.86,
      468.38
    ],
    "text": "Clause 5 : This clause inserts sections 6A and 6B in the principal enactment and the legaleffect is to empower the Minsiter in charge of the subject of Buddha Sasana and ReligiousAffairs to declare areas as \u201cSacred Areas\u201d in terms of the Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      479.11,
      455.87,
      498.14
    ],
    "text": "Clause 6 : This clause amends section 21 of the principal enactment and the legal effect ofthe section as amended is consequential to the amendment made by clause 4 of the Bill.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.83,
      508.87,
      455.89,
      527.78
    ],
    "text": "Clause 7 : This clause makes provision for the validation of certain acts carried out underthe provision of section 6 of the Act, prior to its amendment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman",
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
